      <div purpose="landing-page-section">
        <div purpose="section-heading">
          <h3>What you get with Fleet on-premise</h3>
          <p>Fleet's self-hosted deployment gives your security and compliance teams everything they need without any of the data residency trade-offs of cloud-only MDMs.</p>
        </div>
        <div purpose="feature-cards">
          <div purpose="feature-card">
            <div purpose="card-body">
              <p purpose="card-title">Complete data sovereignty</p>
              <p>Every enrollment record, MDM command, and policy result stays in your database, on your infrastructure, accessible only to your team.</p>
            </div>
            <div purpose="card-footer">
              <p>Fleet never has visibility into your deployment</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-card">
            <div purpose="card-body">
              <p purpose="card-title">Air-gap and offline operation</p>
              <p>Zero outbound internet dependency. Package agents and updates for internal distribution. Designed for classified networks from day one.</p>
            </div>
            <div purpose="card-footer">
              <p>0 external calls required</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-card">
            <div purpose="card-body">
              <p purpose="card-title">100% feature parity</p>
              <p>Not a stripped-down tier. AI-native workflows with human review, declarative device management (DDM), live osquery, and vulnerability management all ship to self-hosted on the same day as Fleet Cloud.</p>
            </div>
            <div purpose="card-footer">
              <p>One codebase, same features everywhere</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-card">
            <div purpose="card-body">
              <p purpose="card-title">Bring your own encryption keys</p>
              <p>Use AWS KMS, HashiCorp Vault, or hardware HSMs. FileVault and BitLocker recovery keys stay in your database. No vendor escrow.</p>
            </div>
            <div purpose="card-footer">
              <p>AWS KMS, Vault, or HSM support</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-card">
            <div purpose="card-body">
              <p purpose="card-title">Your upgrade schedule</p>
              <p>Test in staging, validate, deploy on your timeline. No forced upgrades or surprise API changes, critical for environments where change control is mandatory.</p>
            </div>
            <div purpose="card-footer">
              <p>No forced upgrades or deprecations</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-card">
            <div purpose="card-body">
              <p purpose="card-title">Fully auditable open-source codebase</p>
              <p><a href="/lp/open-source">Public on GitHub</a>. Every line of code touching your device data can be inspected, built from source, and verified by your team. Because the code is public, you can also ask Claude or Copilot how any part of Fleet works.</p>
            </div>
            <div purpose="card-footer">
              <p>No black-box binaries</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
