      <div purpose="landing-page-section">
        <div purpose="section-heading">
          <h3>Frequently asked questions</h3>
        </div>
        <div purpose="faq" class="d-flex flex-column">
          <div purpose="accordion" class="d-flex flex-column justify-content-start">
            <div purpose="accordion-body">
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="onprem-faq__header1" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#onprem-faq__body1" aria-controls="onprem-faq__body1">
                  Where can I deploy Fleet?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="onprem-faq__body1" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="onprem-faq__header1">
                  Anywhere you control: <a href="/docs/deploy/deploy-fleet">on-premises</a>, in any major cloud (AWS, Azure, GCP, DigitalOcean), in containers (Docker, or Kubernetes via Helm or Terraform), or in air-gapped environments. Teams that prefer a managed option can choose Fleet Cloud and get the same features either way.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="onprem-faq__header2" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#onprem-faq__body2" aria-controls="onprem-faq__body2">
                  What infrastructure does a self-hosted Fleet deployment need?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="onprem-faq__body2" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="onprem-faq__header2">
                  Fleet has three infrastructure dependencies: a MySQL database, a Redis-compatible cache (Redis or Valkey), and a TLS certificate. A single Fleet server can handle tens of thousands of hosts, and deployments scale horizontally to hundreds of thousands of devices behind a load balancer.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="onprem-faq__header3" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#onprem-faq__body3" aria-controls="onprem-faq__body3">
                  Can Fleet run in an air-gapped environment?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="onprem-faq__body3" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="onprem-faq__header3">
                  Yes. Fleet has zero outbound internet dependency. Package the Fleet server, agents, and updates for offline deployment, and distribute them through your internal artifact repositories.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="onprem-faq__header4" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#onprem-faq__body4" aria-controls="onprem-faq__body4">
                  Does self-hosted Fleet have the same features as Fleet Cloud?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="onprem-faq__body4" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="onprem-faq__header4">
                  Yes. Fleet is one codebase with one feature set. Every feature available in Fleet Cloud ships to self-hosted on the same day, including AI-native workflows, declarative device management (DDM), live osquery, and vulnerability management.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="onprem-faq__header5" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#onprem-faq__body5" aria-controls="onprem-faq__body5">
                  Can I use AI with self-hosted Fleet?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="onprem-faq__body5" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="onprem-faq__header5">
                  Yes. Fleet works natively with Copilot, Claude, or any AI harness, and you choose which tools your team uses. AI drafts each change against your own Fleet instance, and a person on your team approves it before it touches a device.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="onprem-faq__header6" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#onprem-faq__body6" aria-controls="onprem-faq__body6">
                  Can I set up new Windows PCs without Microsoft licenses?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="onprem-faq__body6" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="onprem-faq__header6">
                  Yes. Fleet gives you an order email. Forward it to Dell, Lenovo, or HP, and they install Fleet before the PC ships. No Autopilot, Entra ID, or Intune is required. See <a href="/windows">Windows device management</a>.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="onprem-faq__header7" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#onprem-faq__body7" aria-controls="onprem-faq__body7">
                  Is Fleet open source?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="onprem-faq__body7" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="onprem-faq__header7">
                  Yes. The majority of Fleet is released under the MIT license, and all of Fleet’s source code is public on GitHub at <a href="https://github.com/fleetdm/fleet" target="_blank">github.com/fleetdm/fleet</a>. A separate set of paid features lives in an <code>/ee</code> directory under a commercial license. See the <a href="/lp/open-source">open source MDM page</a> for the full breakdown.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="d-flex flex-row justify-content-start">
              <p purpose="contact-note">Have another question? <a href="/docs/get-started/faq">Read the full FAQ</a> or <a href="/contact">talk to an engineer</a>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
